<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Afonja</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1817</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Afonja was the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/are-ona-kakanfo">Are-Ona-Kakanfo</a>, the leading military commander of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oyo-empire">Oyo Empire</a>, based at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ilorin">Ilorin</a>. Around c. 1817 he rebelled against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alaafin">Alaafin</a> and enlisted <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fula">Fulani</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hausa">Hausa</a> Muslim support. His rebellion was a decisive blow to Oyo, and Ilorin was soon absorbed into the sphere of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sokoto-caliphate">Sokoto Caliphate</a> after Afonja himself was overthrown by his allies.</p></div>
